  nonce: ec73  # ec73
  data:  # ec73
    kind: invariant  # ec73
    title: "Undeclared custom field keys land silently: the write path checks only required-present, validate warns only for schema-bearing kinds, CI never runs it --strict, and work_item declares no schema at all"  # ec73
    status: violated  # ec73
    priority: 2  # ec73
    parent:  # ec73
    tags:  # ec73
    - tracker  # ec73
    - data_integrity  # ec73
    - cli_input_boundary  # ec73
    isbefore: []  # ec73
    duplicate_of: []  # ec73
    not_duplicate_of: []  # ec73
    pr_ref:  # ec73
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-06 while sweeping the mechanism behind INV-varil (core attribute\nnames accepted as custom keys). That item is the narrow half; this is the\nfamily: an undeclared custom field key lands without anyone being told.\n\nTHE THREE LAYERS THAT EACH FAIL TO SAY SO, read from source at dev 19c80ab74a:\n\n  1. WRITE PATH. Store.add (store.py ~1261) checks only that REQUIRED schema\n     keys are present. Store.update runs no schema check at all: the only\n     fields_schema references in store.py are the add-time required check.\n     `--field` / `--add-field` in cli.py store any key verbatim.\n  2. VALIDATOR. validation.py:_validate_fields_schema reports an unknown key\n     as a WARNING, and only when the kind declares a fields_schema. KindConfig\n     documents the no-schema case as \"accepts arbitrary keys with no\n     validation\" (models.py:443). validate_all applies ONE config to all three\n     tiers.\n  3. THE GATE. .github/workflows/tracker-ci.yml:67, ci.yml:1290 and\n     .woodpecker/woodpecker.yml:320 all run `scripts/tracker validate` with\n     NO --strict. --strict is the only thing that promotes warnings to errors\n     (validation.py:646). Live run today: 26 warnings, \"validation passed\",\n     exit 0.\n\nTHE CORPUS, 2128 items (scripts/tracker --json list, custom keys per kind\nagainst the canonical config's fields_schema):\n\n  invariant (schema: statement, root_cause, fix, verification,\n             regression_tests, dogfood_anon_id)\n      severity        17   undeclared -> WARNED, ignored\n      status/priority/tags/description/pr_ref  3/3/2/1/1  core-name shadows\n                                               (INV-varil) -> WARNED, ignored\n  work_item (NO schema)\n      dogfood_anon_id 20   never reported\n      statement       13   never reported\n      root_cause       5   never reported\n      rationale        4   never reported\n      status/priority/tags/description/isbefore  2/2/2/4/1  core-name shadows\n                                               (INV-varil) -> never reported\n  meta_invariant (schema: statement) -- clean.\n\nWHAT THE CORPUS SAYS ABOUT THE DESIGN. The open dict is USED, and for real\nthings: dogfood_anon_id was a convention first and a declared field second\n(tracker CHANGELOG: added to the invariant schema so items \"render cleanly\ninstead of producing an unknown field warning\"). It is on 20 WORK ITEMS too,\nwhere no schema exists, so the declaration never reached them. `statement` /\n`root_cause` on 13 / 5 work items is the invariant vocabulary being borrowed.\n`severity` (17) is a convention no schema names. Each of these was an agent\nimprovising a key and the tool saying nothing, or saying it where nothing\nreads it. The owner's framing, 2026-09-06: the flexibility \"is also a\nbeautiful way to completely undermine your whole data model and have your\nagent say nothing about it because they are just improvising workarounds\nwilly-nilly\". The corpus above is the measurement of that.\n\nTHE AGENT HALF, from the record: the `--field isbefore=` incident (WI-mifag,\nvalue \"\") was written into LIVE.md sec 2 as an OPERATING RULE (\"use\n--add-isbefore\") and never filed as a mechanism; WI-joruz's misplaced\ndescription was repaired on that one item (ops aac0 / 9285, which blanked the\ncustom key to \"\" and left it) with nothing filed. Both are per-item\nworkarounds standing in for the structural fix.\n\nSIDE FINDING, not claimed here: .agent/tracker-workspace/config.yaml is\nstale relative to .agent/tracker/config.yaml (still allows `holding`, lacks\ndeprecated_statuses and dogfood_anon_id). validate_all reads one config, so\nthe stale copy is a second home (LIVE.md rule 12); whether anything reads it\nis UNCHECKED.\n\nWHAT DISCHARGES THIS -- design is the owner's call; the options, cheapest\nfirst:\n  (a) Make the validator's unknown-key check a write-time check: one predicate\n      shared by Store.add, Store.update and validation.py, so the tool refuses\n      at the moment the key is typed and names the schema.\n  (b) Give work_item a fields_schema, and let each kind declare\n      `additional_fields: reject | warn` (default reject). The candidates the\n      corpus already uses -- rationale, statement, root_cause,\n      dogfood_anon_id, severity -- are the list the owner decides on; an\n      undeclared key then needs a config change, which is a reviewed diff.\n  (c) Run `scripts/tracker validate --strict` in the three CI callers once\n      the corpus is clean, so a regression fails rather than scrolls.\n  (d) Clean the corpus: declare or remove every undeclared key above; the\n      core-name shadows are INV-varil's cleanup.\nPositive control for closure: the census above re-run reads 0 undeclared\nkeys on N items, with N stated, AND a deliberate `--field bogus=1` on a\nthrowaway item is REFUSED (behavioural evidence, not the validator count).\n\nRELATED, NOT DUPLICATE: INV-varil (core-name shadows; holds regardless of\nschema), INV-liram (required-present check, satisfied), WI-lorip\n(--add-field/--remove-field, done)."  # ec73
    fields:  # ec73
      statement: "A custom field key that no kind schema declares must not land without a trace: it is refused at write time, or failed by a validator that a gate actually runs."  # ec73
      root_cause: "Store.add checks only that required schema keys are present and Store.update runs no schema check; validation.py reports an unknown key as a WARNING and only when the kind declares a fields_schema; the three CI workflows run scripts/tracker validate without --strict so warnings pass; work_item declares no fields_schema, which KindConfig documents as accepting arbitrary keys with no validation."  # ec73
